Let \(f:X	o Y\) and \(g:Y	o Z\) be strictly differentiable at \( ar x\) and \( ar y=f( ar x)\), respectively, between finite-dimensional spaces. With \( ar z=g( ar y)\), \[D^*(g\circ f)( ar x, ar z)(z^*)=\{
abla f( ar x)^*
abla g( ar y)^*z^*\}=\{
abla(g\circ f)( ar x)^*z^*\}\quad(z^*\in Z^*).\]

For every \(u\in\mathbb R^{n}\), the composite has the singleton second-order subdifferential \[\partial^{2}g( ar x,
abla g( ar x))(u)=\{
abla^{2}g( ar x)u\}.\] Its Hessian-vector product is given by \[
abla^{2}g( ar x)u=JF( ar x)^{\mathsf T}
abla^{2}h(F( ar x))JF( ar x)u+\sum_{i=1}^{m} rac{\partial h}{\partial y_i}(F( ar x))
abla^{2}F_i( ar x)u.\]
